  {
    "label_id": "L-029",
    "x": 4843.478254517613,
    "y": 1898.2659899666087,
    "rotation": 0.0,
    "text": "1 For not simple requests Patch,Put,Delete - Browser sends ACCESS-CONTROL-REQUEST headers 2 Server checks that headers and respond without body, just with ACCESS-CONTROL-ALLOW headers and 3 that headers must match the headers that browser has sent, if not - no request happen 1 So for simple requests with simple methods/headers - we get no preflight request - and browser sends the request rightaway with ACCESS-CONTROL-REQUEST headers It means that that request may reach the server and server may act 2 But server must include ACCESS-CONTROL-ALLOW headers 3 Browser compares headers and if there is a mismatch - js cant read the response"
  },
  {
    "label_id": "L-030",
    "x": 5114.75175477948,
    "y": 2651.1504144656847,
    "rotation": 0.0,
    "text": "about csrf - so if the request is simple enough cors may not help against csrf, but we usually deal with json which is not a simple content type and causes preflight, even if cookies and cred included by itself dont cause preflight"
  },
  {
    "label_id": "L-031",
